  agent_test_prompt: "Please test how FengSui works with this router ({model}) and write a report I can send to its developers.\n1. Use FengSui's MCP tools only. Never reach or log in to the router directly for this: it allows one admin session at a time, and wrong passwords lock it.\n2. Start read-only: call get_cpe_session_status, get_device_report, get_cpe_telemetry, list_neighbor_cells, list_terminal_topology, get_router_settings, get_access_control and get_sms_status, and note for each whether it worked, failed (with the error code) or came back empty.\n3. I have turned on what the test needs in FengSui. Ask me before any write test and say what it could do. If you cannot see lock_band, reconnect_cellular, reboot_cpe or probe_router_endpoints, ask me to reconnect FengSui's MCP server (in Claude Code: /mcp); if they are still missing, ask me to check under Settings → Device whether that write is turned off or not on this router, and to choose \"Copy prompt and start test\" again. Skip a write that is off or missing, and say so in the report.\n4. You reach the internet through this router, so never cut yourself off: lock only the LTE bands get_cpe_telemetry shows in use and put things back right after (no lock before: unlock with unlock_rf_locks; a lock before: lock those bands again; should the WAN stay down 3 minutes, FengSui writes back the setting from before the lock); a reconnect drops the line for tens of seconds and a reboot for a minute or two, so ask me first; there is no MCP tool for the mobile data switch, so skip it.\n5. If you have send_sms, test SMS: ask me for a number, send one test SMS (this one only; my plan charges for it) and ask me to reply to it from my phone; once the reply has synced (sync_sms helps), mark it read with mark_sms_read, then delete both test messages with delete_sms (they go to FengSui's Recently deleted, where they can be restored). Leave every other message alone. Without send_sms, skip SMS.\n6. After each write, call get_device_report and read the read-back in the recent write results (match means the router took it).\n7. When done, check the connection works. Do not change the settings the test turned on yourself: if every write read back as a match, tell me these features work on this router; if something failed, tell me which write, and remind me to turn that one off under Settings → Device. Then remind me to choose \"End test\" there, which puts back the settings from before the test in one go.\n8. On a Huawei HiLink router (skip this step on another brand), use probe_router_endpoints to find, on this router, the endpoints FengSui is missing: take the Huawei HiLink endpoint names you know (such as the GET endpoints of huawei-lte-api) as candidates, at most 12 per call and at least 10 s between calls. It sends only GETs, inside FengSui's session, and returns structure, never a value; paths that would change the router are refused, so do not retry them in another spelling. Add every endpoint with known: false and state: supported, with its structure, under \"Other findings\", and say what feature it may belong to; include anything unexpected a tool returned.\n9. The report: model, firmware, the result of each read and write, error codes, other findings. Never include an IMEI, IMSI, phone number, IP or MAC address, cell ID or SMS text; get_device_report's report and probe_router_endpoints' structures are already desensitized and may be attached whole.\n10. Finally give me the issue link and the text to paste, for me to check and post myself: {issueUrl}",
